    "Most adults need about seven to nine hours of sleep each night. That is roughly a third of our lives, so it must be doing something important.",
    "While we sleep, the brain moves through cycles of light, deep, and dream sleep, each lasting about ninety minutes. Every stage has a different job.",
    "In deep sleep, the body repairs tissue, and research suggests the brain clears out waste from the day. It is like a night crew cleaning a busy city.",
    "In dream sleep, the brain sorts the day’s experiences, keeping what matters and letting go of the rest. This is how today’s lessons become tomorrow’s memories.",
    "Skip these stages and the costs show up fast. Attention drops, reaction time slows, and mood swings become more likely, even after just one short night.",
    "Over weeks, chronic sleep loss is linked to higher health risks, from weaker immunity to heart disease. That is why sleep is not a luxury.",
    "The good news is that small habits help. Keep a regular schedule, dim the lights an hour before bed, and keep screens out of reach.",
